    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nRunning with the cython master branch I see compilation failures trying to build apache/arrow.  I bisected the failures back to\n\n```\n(cp315t) ~/s/p/c/cython 3.3.0a1-48-g43bf9d98e|BISECTING|✓\n✔ 17:39:36 [belanna] @ git bisect good\n95c0c67fe2083031c387cbdefb5853e5623dc96b is the first 'bad' commit\ncommit 95c0c67fe2083031c387cbdefb5853e5623dc96b\nAuthor: Stefan Behnel <stefan_ml@behnel.de>\nDate:   Sun Jul 5 18:35:27 2026 +0200\n\n    Infer exception base types (GH-7783)\n\n    Teaches Cython about Python's exception class hierarchy and allows it to\n    infer a concrete exception (base) type as spanning type for two given exceptions.\n\n    Moves the long list of known builtin type names from `Code.py` (where it\n    always felt awkward) to `PyrexTypes.py`. `Builtin.py` might seem better\n    but introduces import order issues since the list is used in other\n    modules that `Builtin.py` depends on. It now lives right before\n    `BuiltinObjectType` in `PyrexTypes.py`, which seems sufficiently appropriate.\n\n    I also moved `uncachable_builtins` with it to help keeping that set in sight of the known builtins.\n    I wonder if `renamed_py2_builtins_map` should be moved as well. It's not going to change any more.\n\n Cython/Compiler/Builtin.py             |  76 ++++++++++++++++----\n Cython/Compiler/Code.py                | 189 --------------------------------------------------\n Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py           |   4 +-\n Cython/Compiler/Nodes.py               |  23 ++++---\n Cython/Compiler/PyrexTypes.py          | 378 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----\n Cython/Compiler/Symtab.py              |   8 +--\n Cython/Compiler/Tests/TestBuiltin.py   |  29 +++++++-\n Cython/Compiler/Tests/TestTypes.py     |   1 +\n Cython/Utility/Builtins.c              | 113 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n docs/src/userguide/extension_types.rst |  23 +++++++\n tests/run/builtin_exceptions.py        | 216 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n tests/run/type_inference.pyx           |  60 ++++++++++++++++\n 12 files changed, 882 insertions(+), 238 deletions(-)\n```\n\n\n```\n<...>\n  [56/67] Building CXX object CMakeFiles/lib.dir/lib.cpp.o\n  FAILED: [code=1] CMakeFiles/lib.dir/lib.cpp.o\n  /usr/bin/ccache /usr/bin/g++ -DARROW_HAVE_RUNTIME_AVX2 -DARROW_HAVE_RUNTIME_AVX512 -DARROW_HAVE_RUNTIME_BMI2 -DARROW_HAVE_RUNTIME_SSE4_2 -DARROW_HAVE_SSE4_2 -Dlib_EXPORTS -I/home/tcaswell/.pybuild/cp315t/include/python3.16t -I/home/tcaswell/source/p/apache/arrow/python/pyarrow/src -I/tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/pyarrow/src -I/home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/include -I/home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/lib/python3.16t/site-packages/numpy/_core/include -Wno-noexcept-type -Wno-self-move  -Wall -fno-semantic-interposition -msse4.2  -fdiagnostics-color=always  -fno-omit-frame-pointer -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-maybe-uninitialized -O3 -DNDEBUG -O2 -ftree-vectorize  -std=c++20 -fPIC -Wno-unused-function -MD -MT CMakeFiles/lib.dir/lib.cpp.o -MF CMakeFiles/lib.dir/lib.cpp.o.d -o CMakeFiles/lib.dir/lib.cpp.o -c /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp: In function ‘PyObject* __pyx_pf_7pyarrow_3lib_28set_timezone_db_path(PyObject*, PyObject*)’:\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:33814:21: warning: ‘arrow::GlobalOptions::timezone_db_path’ is deprecated: Deprecated in 24.0.0. Only needed for Clang/libc++ on Windows. [-Wdeprecated-declarations]\n  33814 |     __pyx_v_options.timezone_db_path = ((std::optional<std::string> )((std::string)__pyx_t_7));\n        |                     ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  In file included from /home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/include/arrow/api.h:29,\n                   from /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:1440:\n  /home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/include/arrow/config.h:102:30: note: declared here\n    102 |   std::optional<std::string> timezone_db_path;\n        |                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:33814:21: warning: ‘arrow::GlobalOptions::timezone_db_path’ is deprecated: Deprecated in 24.0.0. Only needed for Clang/libc++ on Windows. [-Wdeprecated-declarations]\n  33814 |     __pyx_v_options.timezone_db_path = ((std::optional<std::string> )((std::string)__pyx_t_7));\n        |                     ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/include/arrow/config.h:102:30: note: declared here\n    102 |   std::optional<std::string> timezone_db_path;\n        |                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:33814:21: warning: ‘arrow::GlobalOptions::timezone_db_path’ is deprecated: Deprecated in 24.0.0. Only needed for Clang/libc++ on Windows. [-Wdeprecated-declarations]\n  33814 |     __pyx_v_options.timezone_db_path = ((std::optional<std::string> )((std::string)__pyx_t_7));\n        |                     ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /home/tcaswell/.virtualenvs/cp315t/include/arrow/config.h:102:30: note: declared here\n    102 |   std::optional<std::string> timezone_db_path;\n        |                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp: In function ‘PyObject* __pyx_pf_7pyarrow_3lib_9MapScalar___getitem__(__pyx_obj_7pyarrow_3lib_MapScalar*, PyObject*)’:\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:113612:24: error: ‘__Pyx_PyExc_LookupError_Check’ was not declared in this scope\n  113612 |           if (!(likely(__Pyx_PyExc_LookupError_Check(__pyx_t_3)) || __Pyx_RaiseUnexpectedTypeError(\"LookupError\", __pyx_t_3))) __PYX_ERR(3, 1192, __pyx_L1_error)\n         |                        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:1717:43: note: in definition of macro ‘likely’\n   1717 |   #define likely(x)   __builtin_expect(!!(x), 1)\n        |                                           ^\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:113625:24: error: ‘__Pyx_PyExc_LookupError_Check’ was not declared in this scope\n  113625 |           if (!(likely(__Pyx_PyExc_LookupError_Check(__pyx_t_3)) || __Pyx_RaiseUnexpectedTypeError(\"LookupError\", __pyx_t_3))) __PYX_ERR(3, 1192, __pyx_L1_error)\n         |                        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /tmp/tmp6nlbqd7k/build/lib.cpp:1717:43: note: in definition of macro ‘likely’\n   1717 |   #define likely(x)   __builtin_expect(!!(x), 1)\n        |                                           ^\n<...>\n```\n\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nI discovered this trying to install apache arrow.  I did the bisect by hand and then asked the robot (opus 4.8) to generate a minimal reproducer and it came up with\n\n```cython\n# cython: language_level=3\n\ndef raise_lookup(i):\n    raise IndexError(i) if isinstance(i, int) else KeyError(i)\n```\n\nwhich I confirmed generates code that compiles on on 3.2.9 and fails on 95c0c67fe2083031c387cbdefb5853e5623dc96b\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nclean compile \n\n### OS\n\nlinux\n\n### Python version\n\nmain branch and 3.14 branch\n\n### Cython version\n\nmaster\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
